    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1133">

                <pb facs="0334" n="2036" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p2/pg2036"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">774.5/3–2453: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1133<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        the United Kingdom</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1133-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top
                            secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-03-24T18:36:00-05:00">March 24, 1953—6:36
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6343. For your information US views on British note contained in Deptel 1883
                    presented to British in writing inform contained above reftel in three
                    paragraphs in middle of message immediately subsequent to the phrase “End
                    Verbatim Text.” British were not shown copy of personal message from the
                    President to Naguib but were given orally summary of points it covered. We felt
                    it improper show text to British and were fearful of leak that personal
                    confidential <pb facs="0335" n="2037" xml:id="pg2037"/> message to head of third
                    State had been coordinated with them.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Dulles</hi></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1133-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1133-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated priority to Cairo as telegram 1885. Drafted and approved by Byroade.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
